			"51": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 4: INSTANCED MATERIALS\n\nIn this final example we use instanced colors from the Gradient Palette node to create multiple materials.\nJust like all other types, materials get repeated when the collection of materials is smaller than the instance count of the collection it is applied to.\n\nIn this case we have 64 transformations and only 8 materials. \n64\/8 = 8 repetitions, which gives us nice stacks of colored hexagons."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 1044.76611328125,
					"width": 1994.813720703125,
					"x": 258.6077880859375,
					"y": 1945.8363037109375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ff2dc18a",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"52": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: TEXTURE'S & BLEND MODES\n\nIn this example we're projecting the star, onto the mesh.\nFirst we create the shape, next we turn it into a texture with the Shape Render.\nNext, we create a material out of it.\nNote how the Shape Render and Texture Material node each have their own color.\nNow try the different blend modes to see how they affect each other."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 582.0252685546875,
					"width": 1515.0767822265625,
					"x": 258.6077880859375,
					"y": 675.88836669921875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffe53357",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"53": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TEXTURE MATERIAL\n\nThe Texture Material node constructs a material type out  of colors and\/or textures.\nWrap and blend modes can be defined by the user.\n\nThe materials can be applied to either the Mesh2D or Slice Render node."
					}
				},
